# What ships is the bundle, the manifest, the README and the icon. Nothing else.
#
# Without this file vsce packages the whole working tree: the last build was 634 KB, of which
# 1.3 MB uncompressed was `.claude/` — the planning documents, which describe internal architecture
# and reference customer data, and which have no business being handed to anyone who installs the
# extension. `src/` went too, which is 180 KB of source that `dist/extension.js` already contains.

.claude/**
.github/**
.vscode/**
src/**
node_modules/**

# Build inputs and repo furniture, none of which the extension host reads.
tsconfig.json
biome.json
bun.lock
bun.lockb
CLAUDE.md
.gitignore
.editorconfig
*.vsix

# The bundle is what runs; its map would only leak paths.
dist/**/*.map
